Thanks a lot for looking into this in depth. Yes, there are two code paths
that use the hardware differently. The multi-color case is actually the
more complicated one, using modulation to color the same texture many
times, so it's surprising that it works, while the simpler case is broken.
One possible test is to use white, so that the glyph image is exactly the
same in both cases. That would eliminate one difference at least.

Michael

